{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift#L24","fileName":"UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift"},"externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule010UndirectedaB0V","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same edge as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". Each slot has a row of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges; each edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop twice in its vertex’s row (as Boost stores it)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The rows share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many vertices it has. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position (open addressing with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiplicative hash, not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":"’s SipHash) answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1) expected."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/undirectedadjacencylist"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph stored as adjacency lists: the undirected counterpart of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacency_list<…, undirectedS>"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-17f2v","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2o9bq","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyList